From 00c508bcecfb5a725cc6e36628eb92690c7f926a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andree Toonk <andree@toonk.io>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 19:16:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/13] tcp: process an uncontended connection's segments
 inline

tcp.InlineProcessing handles a segment for an established, uncontended
endpoint on the goroutine that delivered it (a TryLock and
handleSegmentsLocked) instead of queueing it for a processor goroutine,
only when the flags carry no SYN, RST or FIN and the state stays
ESTABLISHED. tcp.BatchProcessing runs the work the inline path cannot
take (a listener's SYN and the handshake, FIN, close) on the delivering
goroutine after the batch, through tcp.DrainDeferred. tcp.TxHashFromRx
copies the receive queue into the connection's transmit hash so replies
leave on the queue the receive goroutine owns. The handoff to a processor
goroutine was one wakeup per request: 458k to 661k req/s at the time.
